{"text": "You'd think the flood starts there. It doesn't. By 1900 — sixty years on — the world's whole haul: about sixty parallaxes. Sixty known distances, in your galaxy of billions. The flood came when the measuring left the ground. A satellite called hip-AR-koss pinned down a hundred and eighteen thousand stars in the 1990s. Only about one in six had an error under ten percent. Then came GUY-uh, a European craft. From 2013 to 2025 it scanned the sky and measured more than a billion stars. At its sharpest — on paper — it reads your two-euro coin from seven hundred and fifty-nine thousand kilometres. Twice as far as the Moon. And still your triangle runs out inside your own galaxy. The Milky Way spans some eighty-seven thousand light-years, give or take a few thousand. For most stars, GUY-uh's sharp reach covers a slice of that. Build a bigger telescope. The base of your triangle has not grown a metre. Past a point, the jump is smaller than the blur.", "alignment": {"characters": ["Y", "o", "u", "'", "d", " ", "t", "h", "i", "n", "k", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "l", "o", "o", "d", " ", "s", "t", "a", "r", "t", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", "r", "e", ".", " ", "I", "t", " ", "d", "o", "e", "s", "n", "'", "t", ".", " ", "B", "y", " ", "1", "9", "0", "0", " ", "—", " ", "s", "i", "x", "t", "y", " ", "y", "e", "a", "r", "s", " ", "o", "n", " ", "—", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "w", "o", "r", "l", "d", "'", "s", " ", "w", "h", "o", "l", "e", " ", "h", "a", "u", "l", ":", " ", "a", "b", "o", "u", "t", " ", "s", "i", "x", "t", "y", " ", "p", "a", "r", "a", "l", "l", "a", "x", "e", "s", ".", " ", "S", "i", "x", "t", "y", " ", "k", "n", "o", "w", "n", " ", "d", "i", "s", "t", "a", "n", "c", "e", "s", ",", " ", "i", "n", " ", "y", "o", "u", "r", " ", "g", "a", "l", "a", "x", "y", " ", "o", "f", " ", "b", "i", "l", "l", "i", "o", "n", "s", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "f", "l", "o", "o", "d", " ", "c", "a", "m", "e", " ", "w", "h", "e", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "m", "e", "a"